#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087487 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/id #uuid "03bb8d2d-55c5-5511-94c5-73e73db9ccf8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5361" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x+1)^2}{10} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1$." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) - \\frac{y^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) - \\frac{0^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n((x + 1)^{2})/(10) &= 1 \\\\\n(x + 1)^{2} &= 10 \\\\\nx + 1 &= ± \\sqrt{10} \\\\\nx &= -1 ± \\sqrt{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are\n\n$$\n\\left(-1\\pm \\sqrt{10},0\\right)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087488 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "395f435d-473f-5dae-b215-2986556d5793" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Hyperbola and a Horizontal or Vertical Line"}] :question/id #uuid "b3eac4e2-5e85-5669-8dfb-c7fe4e5a47ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-5362" :question/problem "Calculate the points where the hyperbola\n$\\dfrac{x^2}{10}-\\dfrac{y^2}{15}=1$\nintersects the line $y=-3$." :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-3$, we substitute $y=-3$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{y^{2}}{15} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - ((-3)^{2})/(15) &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{9}{15} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{10} - \\frac{3}{5} &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} - 6 &= 10 \\\\\nx^{2} &= 16 \\\\\nx &= ± 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the hyperbola intersects the horizontal line $y=-3$ at the points $(\\pm 4, -3)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087564 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c249cf3a-7864-5132-80fa-c18a3ea915c2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/id #uuid "bb09b5f0-832f-5008-970c-87c6dfaf076f" :question/math-academy-id "e-7424" :question/problem "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $7y^2 -5x^2 = 28$." :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7y^{2} - 5x^{2} &= 28 \\\\\n7y^{2} - 5(0)^{2} &= 28 \\\\\n7y^{2} &= 28 \\\\\ny^{2} &= 4 \\\\\ny &= ± 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 2)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087565 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Hyperbola and a Line"}] :question/id #uuid "0704ee42-bc8c-5d98-b6f2-ad952ab41560" :question/math-academy-id "e-7425" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{9} - \\dfrac{y^2}{25}=1$ intersects the line $y = x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/874/Source/Images/39c8aedbe6ab698c5a77db42509d3ef3.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x$, we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{x^{2}}{9} - \\frac{y^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{9} - \\frac{x^{2}}{25} &= 1 \\\\\n\\frac{16x^{2}}{225} &= 1 \\\\\nx^{2} &= \\frac{225}{16} \\\\\nx &= ± \\frac{15}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c249cf3a-7864-5132-80fa-c18a3ea915c2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5223c88d-2bed-518e-ab79-739ab19ef2be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\pm 5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264704} {:answer/id #uuid "5c0f8a10-32d0-5273-b4d2-ac6c5448dd87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\pm 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264705} {:answer/id #uuid "abfe4fc4-b0b1-5c16-a8f6-95d6252f776e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\pm 15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264706} {:answer/id #uuid "d57c6ea3-bbf5-5f79-bea0-f2b99c839c78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\pm 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264707} {:answer/id #uuid "130b9090-0104-5310-a192-f4f7d09924a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\pm 4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c0f8a10-32d0-5273-b4d2-ac6c5448dd87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\pm 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264705} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1a23922-a622-5033-9716-42a59cd05aaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264703}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6197359c-bb32-5d0b-9b73-5f25f3b8884f" :question/math-academy-id "q-10484" :question/problem "Calculate the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $25{y}^{2}-9{x}^{2}=225.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{y}^{2}-9{x}^{2} & =225 \\\\ 25{y}^{2}-9(0)^{2} & =225 \\\\ 25{y}^{2} & =225 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =9 \\\\ y & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,\\pm 3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "55a53010-eddc-5115-8c70-0f32d0144384" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points of Intersection of a Hyperbola and a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ebe3719-6b6c-517b-8e76-8f5d83710c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264711} {:answer/id #uuid "7f1db45f-077e-5add-b574-bc4b6678098a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264712} {:answer/id #uuid "1074f632-a3ec-55b4-b8e1-db665cc9fe57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264713} {:answer/id #uuid "0c64b342-8f57-57c4-87db-cd82318080f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264714} {:answer/id #uuid "6b5628a9-bccb-561d-a95c-9beeab906454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ebe3719-6b6c-517b-8e76-8f5d83710c62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\pm 2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264711} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c6b3734-dcc2-5602-a1ba-352b66ce175d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264710}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f5d157d-1c5b-55af-87fc-77c12ab18085" :question/math-academy-id "q-10492" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}=1$\nintersects the line $y=x.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{5{x}^{2}}{20}-\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{20} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{20} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =20 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2837bb9-59d4-5af0-b9d3-f4fa9f015599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm 2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264718} {:answer/id #uuid "293104c5-e0ad-53f2-bad3-c2de46f15a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no $x$-intercepts" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264719} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5221c6-21c8-5cff-bbc4-5ad1de77354e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm \\sqrt{2},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264720} {:answer/id #uuid "7f00ad1f-cc4b-5dd7-a1a0-f891b9f4292f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm \\frac{1}{5},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264721} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe8027f-f491-51a7-b341-bf564c5f89dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm \\sqrt{5},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2837bb9-59d4-5af0-b9d3-f4fa9f015599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm 2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264718} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ca0ebf6-e63f-5bb1-b180-9c49f4fabbb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264717}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0582fa2b-c02a-5efe-af39-d631ed443100" :question/math-academy-id "q-170552" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $10{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=40.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =40 \\\\ 10{x}^{2}-(0)^{2} & =40 \\\\ 10{x}^{2}-0 & =40 \\\\ 10{x}^{2} & =40 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $(\\pm 2,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5b62e75-fe55-5dd8-ba67-6f8072a59f77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm 3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264725} {:answer/id #uuid "7c0d19a8-3f5a-5030-873a-ba1fb5fc0101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm 2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264726} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e809c5-9b3c-501d-b9cd-dfd1d06541bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm \\frac{7}{3},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264727} {:answer/id #uuid "f7885174-f6db-50ac-84aa-eab08bd1563d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\pm \\frac{7}{6},0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264728} {:answer/id #uuid "addbf3aa-b105-5118-b1f6-8258cc359713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no $x$-intercepts" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "addbf3aa-b105-5118-b1f6-8258cc359713" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no $x$-intercepts" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264729} :answer-field/id #uuid "02bfe1e6-d148-5f20-8950-68cfb0c6e0ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264724}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3e56066-2a43-5527-b49e-536f49527adc" :question/math-academy-id "q-170553" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola $2(y+3)^{2}-3{x}^{2}=21.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(y+3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(0+3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(3)^{2}-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 2(9)-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ 18-3{x}^{2} & =21 \\\\ -3{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe cannot take the square root of a negative number. Therefore, the equation has no real solutions. So, there are no $x$-intercepts."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cc5c806-dd24-5c3c-a89e-92864116a934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0cc5c806-dd24-5c3c-a89e-92864116a934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264732} :answer-field/id #uuid "8922b141-39c7-5010-89f9-e0e8d5347a98" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264731} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcc35d1c-d56c-5021-ae39-15ec4cbbc93f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc35d1c-d56c-5021-ae39-15ec4cbbc93f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264734} :answer-field/id #uuid "56aae14e-4665-5566-bdb9-625558334861" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264733}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b674bc0-9200-5895-bd90-f0429ce87f8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-277801" :question/problem "The $x$-intercept of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}=1$ is$\\,(${{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16} & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x-1 & =0 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $(1,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c249cf3a-7864-5132-80fa-c18a3ea915c2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Y-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d09b0e76-0168-5cde-95ad-0e066947d8c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d09b0e76-0168-5cde-95ad-0e066947d8c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264737} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a522786-048e-5ef5-a700-46e124f3f508" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75ca9cca-91a3-51ca-b659-eb9dcec3c031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75ca9cca-91a3-51ca-b659-eb9dcec3c031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264739} :answer-field/id #uuid "45927ed7-9b0a-57db-8199-0ffeb029c69f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264738} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67843bb5-458d-5d0c-8ea9-dee271567bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67843bb5-458d-5d0c-8ea9-dee271567bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264741} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef11edb-6168-583a-a677-953c3d40b7de" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5d8a669-aac2-5c1f-8357-29f70e4809b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5d8a669-aac2-5c1f-8357-29f70e4809b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264743} :answer-field/id #uuid "38224f51-3a4a-56bb-ac3b-bf80feaa664a" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264742}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9dfffee-93ab-5b9a-91d2-b8ba63f7d71c" :question/math-academy-id "q-277802" :question/problem "From **top to bottom,** the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}=36$ are\n\n$($\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}} $)\\,$\nand\n$\\,($\n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}} $).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts of the hyperbola, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-4(0)^{2} & =36 \\\\ 9{y}^{2} & =36 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ y & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the $y$-intercepts are $(0,2)$ and $(0,-2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186264744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2de185a6-24a0-55aa-905d-8893a555e331" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the X-Intercepts of a Hyperbola"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cff4a322-0085-569e-9b3f-cef63b861973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264746} {:answer/id #uuid "ef877e01-8fa9-5d5c-97ff-005c48e0c948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cff4a322-0085-569e-9b3f-cef63b861973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264746} :answer-field/id #uuid 